course: dictionary
lesson: 10309
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Look at the words around it first. «Sun cream should be put on again at least every 2 hours and after sweating hard or towelling, because sweat and towels wipe it off.» The sentence is about wiping, so towelling here means rubbing yourself dry.
explain: Towelling can also mean the cloth itself. It is thick, soft and absorbent, which means it soaks up water well. That is why it is used for towels, bathrobes and baby bibs.
explain: Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence. If «rubbing yourself dry» makes sense, you have the right meaning. If the sentence is about a robe or a bib, it means the cloth.
fact: Towelling is a thick, soft, absorbent cotton cloth with little loops.
fact: Absorbent means it soaks up water easily.
fact: «Towelling» can also mean a rub with a towel to dry yourself.
fact: «Towelling robe» means a dressing gown made of towelling. Usually we say some towelling, not a towelling, when we mean the cloth. In American English it is spelt toweling.
fact: Old, informal: a towelling once meant a beating. You will rarely see it used like this now, so the context will tell you.
exercise: «Sun cream should be put on again after sweating hard or towelling.» In this sentence, what does towelling mean? | A sunny day at the beach | A thick, soft cloth for making bibs | *A rub with a towel to dry yourself | A kind of sun cream
exercise: Which item is usually made of towelling? | A pencil | *A bathrobe | A glass of water | A wooden spoon
exercise: What does «absorbent» suggest about towelling? | It is very heavy | *It soaks up water well | It pushes water away | It is made of metal
test: What does «a towelling robe» mean? | A shiny metal jacket | *A dressing gown made of towelling | A robe to wear in a swimming race | A stone cloak
test: Which clue in «because sweat and towels wipe it off» shows that towelling means drying? | Every 2 hours | *Wipe it off | Sun cream | Put on again
exam: Which sentence uses towelling to mean the cloth? | *She wore a soft towelling robe after her swim. | The sun cream was wiped off with a towelling. | She gave her hair a quick towelling after her swim.
